
# Dead links on the rustdoc site that stay: the built-site link gate's freeze, read by docs.yml (link-allow).
# Two causes, both a dependency's doc text that rustdoc copies into a blanket impl on our pages. tracing 0.1.44 writes
# `[default]: dispatcher#setting-the-default-subscriber` as a plain relative URL in `WithSubscriber`'s method docs
# (instrument.rs), so `impl<T> WithSubscriber for T` on each type page links `<module>/dispatcher`: one key per module
# of the renderer, the GUI and the CLI, so every new module with a type adds one here. burn's `Module`, on YoloTiny,
# links `ModuleMapper` and `ModuleVisitor` (2 keys). wasm-bindgen's hidden `WasmDescribe` and `WasmDescribeVector`
# impls on vision_core_web's exported types link `#tymethod.*` anchors rustdoc never renders (4 keys).
# Format: missing<TAB><path> or anchor<TAB><path>#<id>, as verify_site_links.py --print-keys prints it.
# Two-way: a key that resolves now is STALE.
# third_party/ANTfrastructure/docs/docs-sites.md#the-built-site-link-gate

anchor	kataglyphis_vision_core_web/struct.Mapping.html#tymethod.describe
anchor	kataglyphis_vision_core_web/struct.Mapping.html#tymethod.describe_vector
anchor	kataglyphis_vision_core_web/struct.Preprocessor.html#tymethod.describe
anchor	kataglyphis_vision_core_web/struct.Preprocessor.html#tymethod.describe_vector
missing	kataglyphis_burn_demos/yolo/ModuleMapper
